From ec60a9f5a730991f1432979bb63ff7cf4caa985f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:39:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(update): sync fleet-restart scope, marker settlement,
 macOS swap and cron status docs

Four update/fleet statements no longer match main:

- hermes_cli/AGENTS.md, Restart-per-kind: the fleet pass restarts
  hermes-serve* and hermes-dashboard* units as well as hermes-gateway*
  (_is_hermes_gateway_unit, #125297), and the SIGUSR1 drain is gateway-only
  (_service_unit_supports_graceful_sigusr1_restart); serve/dashboard units
  get a plain restart.
- updating.md: "Legacy markers without an inventory ... cannot be
  automatically cleared" contradicts both the page's own earlier paragraph
  and _marker_only_restart_obsolete(), which discharges an inventory-less
  marker once every live gateway runs the current checkout (#115638,
  #125952). What stays fail-closed is a malformed/unsupported inventory, or
  an inventory recorded without its target SHA.
- updating.md, Desktop rebuild: _install_rebuilt_macos_bundles() refuses to
  replace a publisher-signed (Team ID) app with a locally signed rebuild, or
  one with a different Team ID / bundle identifier, and reports it
  (_macos_signing_downgrade_error, #123748).
- multi-profile-gateways.md: with no host gateway, cron_status() first names
  a fresh in-process hermes serve / Desktop backend ticker before telling
  the user to start the host gateway.
